# Code Formatting and Style

## Core Principles
- Write clean, simple, and readable code. Maintain consistency across the codebase.
- Keep files focused on a single responsibility. Aim for shorter files where practical (e.g., under 500 lines including comments).
- Use clear, descriptive, and consistent naming conventions for variables, functions, classes, and files.

## Language
- Use clear and easy-to-understand language in code, comments, and documentation.
- Prefer short, direct sentences.